      "question": "What should I look for when buying a house?",
      "answer": "Look for visible water stains and check the flood map during initial property showings. Check system ages as well as property tax histories. For managed communities, examine association rules and HOA dues. Use our detailed [home inspection checklist](/checklists/home-inspection-checklist/) to guide your physical review."
    },
    {
      "question": "What are the steps in the home buying process?",
      "answer": "The process moves across six distinct milestones starting with budgeting and mortgage pre-approval. You then tour houses, submit an offer with protective contingencies, and complete professional property inspections. The final stretch involves securing homeowners insurance, completing an appraisal, and finalizing loan documents before closing. A seventh phase covers your first week in the house."
